<%#
  "How we matched you" — every answer the user gave, and how the shown results
  measure up.

  This exists for honesty about incomplete data. Most capability fields ship
  empty and fill in only as organizations update their profiles, so a user who
  asked for wheelchair-accessible services would otherwise have no way to tell
  whether these results are accessible or whether nobody has said. Four states,
  because "does not offer this" and "has not told us" are different answers and
  only one of them means the user should look elsewhere.

  Collapsed by default: it is reassurance for the people who want it, not the
  headline. Once opened it STAYS open across "Show more" clicks, which replace
  this panel along with the cards -- see persistent_details_controller.
%>
<% return if criteria.blank? %>

<details class="mb-6 bg-white border rounded-lg border-gray-6 group"
         data-controller="persistent-details"
         data-persistent-details-key-value="smart-match-criteria"
         data-action="toggle->persistent-details#save">
  <summary class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer list-none">
    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-2">
      <%= t("smart_match.results.criteria.title") %>
    </span>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <%# Counts partial matches, not just full ones. Counting only "fully
          matched" read as 1 of 12 even when most criteria were partly met,
          which made the engine look broken rather than selective. %>
      <span class="text-xs font-medium text-gray-4">
        <%= t("smart_match.results.criteria.summary",
              matched: criteria.count(&:matched?), total: criteria.size) %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-gray-4 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
    </span>
  </summary>

  <div class="px-5 pt-1 pb-5 border-t border-gray-6">
    <p class="mt-3 mb-4 text-sm text-gray-4">
      <%= t("smart_match.results.criteria.intro", count: criteria.size) %>
    </p>

    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <% criteria.each do |criterion| %>
        <% style = smart_match_criterion_style(criterion.status) %>
        <li class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 text-sm">
          <span class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="<%= style[:classes] %> font-bold leading-5" aria-hidden="true"><%= style[:icon] %></span>
            <span class="sr-only"><%= style[:aria] %></span>
            <span class="text-gray-2">
              <%= smart_match_criterion_label(criterion.question, criterion.answer) %>
            </span>
          </span>

          <%# Qualitative, not "1 of 3 matches". The raw count invited the
              reading that the engine had failed twice, when a partial match
              across a shortlist is the normal, useful outcome. %>
          <span class="shrink-0 text-xs text-gray-4">
            <%= t("smart_match.results.criteria.status.#{criterion.status}") %>
          </span>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <% if criteria.any? { |c| c.status == "unknown" } %>
      <p class="pt-3 mt-4 text-xs border-t text-gray-4 border-gray-6">
        <%= t("smart_match.results.criteria.unknown_note") %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</details>
